      "raw_answer": "{\n  \"sections\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ownership-helper-relocation\",\n      \"title\": \"Relocate is_owner_or_admin from app/auth.py to new app/ownership.py and re-export it\",\n      \"rationale\": \"All three hunks implement a single access-control concern: moving the per-object ownership check (used to gate /users/<id> read/update and order access) out of the auth module into a dedicated ownership module, while keeping the existing `from app.auth import is_owner_or_admin` import path working via a re-export. Hunk #0 adds the re-export import, hunk #1 removes the original definition, and hunk #0 of ownership.py adds the new definition. The logic is byte-for-byte identical (user.id == owner_id or user.role == 'admin'), so this is a pure refactor of the authorization helper's location rather than a behavior change; the callers in app/routes/users.py (lines 32, 45) and the import in app/routes/orders.py (line 13) depend on the symbol remaining importable from app.auth, which the re-export in hunk #0 preserves.\",\n      \"hunks\": [\n        \"app/auth.py#0\",\n        \"app/auth.py#1\",\n        \"app/ownership.py#0\"\n      ],\n      \"context\": [\n        {\"path\": \"app/routes/users.py\", \"symbol\": \"get_user\", \"start_line\": 28, \"end_line\": 38, \"snapshot\": \"pr\", \"why\": \"Caller that invokes is_owner_or_admin(g.current_user, user_id) to gate profile read access; depends on the symbol staying importable from app.auth\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/routes/users.py\", \"symbol\": \"update_user\", \"start_line\": 41, \"end_line\": 55, \"snapshot\": \"pr\", \"why\": \"Caller that invokes is_owner_or_admin(g.current_user, user_id) to gate profile update access\"},\n        {\"path\": \"app/routes/orders.py\", \"symbol\": \"orders_bp\", \"start_line\": 13, \"end_line\": 13, \"snapshot\": \"pr\", \"why\": \"Imports is_owner_or_admin from app.auth; the re-export in app/auth.py#0 keeps this import valid after the definition moves to app/ownership.py\"},\n        {\"path\": \"security-policy.md\", \"symbol\": \"is_owner_or_admin\", \"start_line\": 18, \"end_line\": 30, \"snapshot\": \"base\", \"why\": \"Policy mandates using is_owner_or_admin(current_user, user_id/order.user_id) for per-object access checks, so the helper must remain available and unchanged in behavior\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
